00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.220
geopolitical tension, let us look at a disciplined framework for staying invested when headlines

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:42.620
scream both fear and euphoria. Market resiliency strategies focus on maintaining core allocations during

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:48.120
periods of short-term euphoria or fear. Markets historically recover from geopolitical shocks and

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:53.040
sentiment extremes, rather than collapsing indefinitely. This approach treats apparent sugar

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.740
highs from positive developments like potential cease fires, not as reasons to chase momentum.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:03.720
Instead, they become signals to rebalance toward high-quality names with durable competitive advantages.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.160
In today's environment of mixed retailer outlooks and elevated macro uncertainty,

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:15.280
the strategy keeps investors from overreacting to headlines. It does so by anchoring decisions to

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.700
weekly moving average trends and free cash flow yields instead of daily price swings.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:25.940
Implementation is straightforward on platforms like Questrade or WellSimple. Scan for companies whose

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:31.240
two-hundred-day moving average has held as support through recent volatility, then deploy capital

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:37.480
in five to ten percent increments within TFSA or RRSP accounts to avoid superficial loss rules.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:43.000
The approach has historically performed best following geopolitical spikes or rapid sentiment shifts.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.380
It delivers outperformance by avoiding whipsaw trades. Primary risks include prolonged drawdowns

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:55.000
if resiliency assumptions prove incorrect. There is also opportunity cost. If markets continue climbing

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:00.240
without pause, staying resilient is one thing, but knowing exactly how options can both protect and

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:05.160
