00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:05.420
to catalyst evaluation. Here is something that most retail investors get wrong about options,

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:10.820
and it cost me money before I figured it out. Imagine you bought protective puts on a broad market

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:18.900
ETF last week when the S&amp;P 500 sat near 7,100 amid rising Iran tensions. Your 710 strike put

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:25.920
filled for a $12 premium on a $700 underlying. Yet the position lost 55% of its value in seven days,

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:32.320
even as the ETF fell 2.8%. Options consist of intrinsic value for a put that is the amount by which

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:38.160
strike exceeds spot price and time value. Theta represents daily decay that typically accelerates from

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:45.980
0.05 to 0.25 per day in the final two weeks before expiration. A covered call involves owning 100 shares

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:51.980
of the underlying and selling and out of the money call. Collecting, for example, $3.50 premium

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:59.040
on a $100 stock boosts annualized income by roughly 3.5% if the call expires worthless.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:08.500
Greeks such as Delta, approximately 0.40 to 0.604 at the money options, indicate 40 to 60% chance

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:14.100
of finishing in the money. Theta helps quantify sensitivity to price and time. The pro-tip,

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:19.580
most retail investors miss is always calculating break even, strike plus net premium for calls,

00:09:19.860 --> 00:09:25.880
or strike minus net premium for puts before entry. Professionals cross-reference implied volatility

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:32.700
rank against the past 30-day realized move. Never risk more than 2-3% of portfolio on any single

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:38.860
options position. The biggest mistake with options is using naked positions that expose portfolios

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:44.860
to theoretically unlimited risk on the short side. Instead, always begin with defined risk structures

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:50.960
like covered calls for income or cash secured puts for entry. Before we wrap, keep an eye on upcoming

